<p><strong>Projects</strong></p>

<hr>

<div class="project-section">
<h3><a href="https://github.com/787-10/CANOPY/">CANOPY: Cross-domain Attribution and Orbital Protection sYstem</a></h3>
<p><strong>May 2026</strong></p>
<p style="margin-top: 10px;">
Edge-deployed multi-domain fusion for space asset defense. Fuses orbital/RF/cyber/PNT/OSINT into a live threat picture, attributes actors via multi-LLM red-teaming, and recommends authorized responses in under 30s on RTX 3090 via local Ollama. Ships with a 51-scenario benchmark for frontier labs to evaluate edge attribution and partner on distillation.
</p>
</div>

<hr>

<div class="project-section">
<h3><a href="https://github.com/787-10/LMAO/">LMAO: Large Multi-Agent Orchestration for Space Robots</a></h3>
<p><strong>Apr. 2026</strong></p>
<p style="margin-top: 10px;">
Distributed robotics framework for resilient space exploration using a hub-and-scout architecture. Enables autonomous multi-agent coordination with onboard fault detection, recovery, and dynamic task replanning, allowing fleets of robots to adapt, self-recover, and continue operating in uncertain, communication-constrained environments.
</p>
</div>

<hr>

<div class="project-section">
<h3><a href="https://rascal.nianet.org/wp-content/uploads/2024-RASC-AL-Technical-Paper-MARA-Stanford-University-with-University-of-Waterloo.pdf">MARA: Modular self-Assembling Robotic Architecture</a></h3>
<p><strong>Dec. 2023 - Jun. 2024</strong></p>
<p style="margin-top: 10px;">
Framework for a self-replicating and self-repairing robotic system designed for asteroid exploration. 
Modules can be independently reconfigured, repaired, and repurposed, enabling autonomous self-assembly, module swapping, and dynamic robot 
reconstruction for maximum system robustness and operational flexibility.
</p>
<p style="margin-top: 10px;">
With in-situ resource utilization on an M-type Asteroid (16 Psyche), MARA can achieve potential launch weight reduction of ~1565 kg.
</p>
</div>

<hr>

<div class="project-section">
<h3><a href="https://github.com/DroneFormer/DroneFormer/">DroneFormer</a></h3>
<p><strong>Feb. 2023</strong></p>
<p style="margin-top: 10px;">
An open-source framework for controlling UAVs using natural language. Leverages Vision-Language-Action models to translate high-level 
natural language commands into low-level drone control code, enabling long-horizon task specification through a no-code interface.
</p>
</div>

<hr>

<div class="project-section">
<h3><a href="https://github.com/787-10/foundamental">Foundamental</a></h3>
<p><strong>Aug. 2025</strong></p>
<p style="margin-top: 10px;">
Track your brand visibility and ranking across different Large Language Models. Monitor how your brand appears in LLM responses 
compared to competitors, with multi-provider support (OpenAI, Ollama, etc.), sentiment analysis, and comprehensive analytics. Built with BAML for 
type-safe, structured LLM interactions.
</p>
<p style="margin-top: 10px;">
Open source alternative to <a href="https://www.tryprofound.com/">Profound</a>.
</p>
</div>

